#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# exp_integral_e

#% text
# `exp_integral_e(nu, x)` gives the generalized exponential integral `E_nu(x)`, the integral of `exp(-x*t)/t^nu` for `t` from 1 to `inf`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The definition is DLMF 8.19.3; `exp_integral_e(1, x)` is `E_1(x)`, `-exp_integral_ei(-x)` for `x > 0`.

#% item
# `exp_integral_e(0, x)` is `exp(-x)/x`. `exp_integral_e(nu, 0)` is `1/(nu - 1)` for `nu > 1`; for `nu <= 1` the integral diverges (`inf` for an inexact `nu`, a pole failure for an exact one).

#% item
# Machine numbers, arbitrary-precision numbers and complex numbers (in the order and in the argument) give numerical values. On the negative real axis the value is that of the principal branch, continuous from above: `E_1(-x)` is `-exp_integral_ei(x) - i pi`.

#% item
# `exp_integral_e` is listable. The derivative in `x` is `-exp_integral_e(nu - 1, x)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
exp_integral_e(1, 1.0)
#% output
#= 0.21938393439552029

#% cell
exp_integral_e(2, 0.5)
#% output
#= 0.326643862324553

#% cell
exp_integral_e(0.5, 2.0)
#% output
#= 0.05702612399289205

#% cell
n(exp_integral_e(1, 1), 30)
#% output
#= 0.21938393439552027367716377546012165

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Several orders:

#% cell
exp_integral_e([1, 2, 3], 1.0)
#% output
#= [0.21938393439552029, 0.14849550677592205, 0.10969196719776014]

#% text
# Special values, exact:

#% cell
[exp_integral_e(0, x), exp_integral_e(0, 2), exp_integral_e(2, 0)]
#% output
#= [exp(-x)/x, 1/(2*exp(2)), 1]

#% text
# Complex arguments, and a complex order:

#% cell
exp_integral_e(1 + 1.0*im, 2 + 3*im)
#% output
#= -0.018943830508373647 + 0.02044377010283004im

#% cell
exp_integral_e(1.5 + 2.0*im, 2.0)
#% output
#= 0.03365764460040722 - 0.01872665558475361im

#% text
# Negative arguments, on the branch cut, and negative orders:

#% cell
exp_integral_e(1, -2.0)
#% output
#= -4.954234356001891 - 3.141592653589793im

#% cell
exp_integral_e(-3, 0.5)
#% output
#= 95.83184423459608

#% text
# Large and small arguments, and large orders:

#% cell
[exp_integral_e(1, 100.0), exp_integral_e(1, 1e-300), exp_integral_e(1000, 3.0)]
#% output
#= [3.683597761682032e-46, 690.1983122333122, 4.968754436630453e-5]

#% text
# 30 digits, at a rational order:

#% cell
n(exp_integral_e(7/3, 5/2), 30)
#% output
#= 0.018489561566471233182890495039224377

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The integral definition:

#% cell
n_integrate(exp(-2*t)/t^3, [t, 1, inf]) - exp_integral_e(3, 2.0)
#% output
#= 9.367506770274758e-17

#% text
# The relation to `exp_integral_ei`:

#% cell
exp_integral_e(1, 2.0) + exp_integral_ei(-2.0)
#% output
#= 0.0

#% text
# The recurrence `nu E_(nu + 1)(x) = exp(-x) - x E_nu(x)`:

#% cell
exp_integral_e(3, 1.5) - (exp(-1.5) - 1.5*exp_integral_e(2, 1.5))/2
#% output
#= 0.0

#% text
# The half order is an error function, `E_(1/2)(x) = sqrt(pi/x) erfc(sqrt(x))`:

#% cell
exp_integral_e(1/2, 2.0) - sqrt(pi/2.0)*erfc(sqrt(2.0))
#% output
#= 3.469446951953614e-17

#% text
# The incomplete gamma function, `E_nu(x) = x^(nu - 1) gamma(1 - nu, x)`:

#% cell
exp_integral_e(3, 0.5) - 0.5^2*gamma(-2, 0.5)
#% output
#= 0.0

#% text
# The derivative:

#% cell
d(exp_integral_e(n, x), x)
#% output
#= -exp_integral_e(-1 + n, x)

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# A symbolic order or argument, and a non-integer exact order at an exact point, stay unevaluated:

#% cell
exp_integral_e(n, x)
#% output
#= exp_integral_e(n, x)

#% cell
exp_integral_e(3/2, 2)
#% output
#= exp_integral_e(3/2, 2)

#% text
# At 0 the integral diverges for `nu <= 1`: an exact order gives a pole failure, an inexact one `inf`:

#% cell
exp_integral_e(1, 0)
#% output
#! failure(pole, exp_integral_e(1, 0))

#% cell
exp_integral_e(1, 0.0)
#% output
#= inf

#% text
# A value below the smallest machine number is 0; an arbitrary-precision argument gives it:

#% cell
exp_integral_e(1, 1000.0)
#% output
#= 0.0

#% cell
n(exp_integral_e(1, 1000), 20)
#% output
#= 5.07089306023516654992720e-438

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `exp_integral_ei`, `gamma`, `log_integral`, `erfc`
